     - <h4>6C Practise multiplying by 10 and 100</h4>
     - <p>Click on the number wheel below. Each time you spin the wheel multiply the number shown by 10, 100 and 1000
     - <p>Choose two numbers from the wheel and record your answer and reason in your learning journal.</p>
     - <p>For example: 64 x 10 = 640, 64 x 100 = 6,400 and 64 x 1000=64,000</p>
     - <p>When you multiply a number by 10, you add a zero to the end of it. So, 64 times 10 is 640.</p>
     - <p>When you multiply a number by 100, you add two zeros to the end of it. So, 64 times 100 is 6400.</p>
     - <p>When you multiply a number by 1000, you add three zeros to the end of it. So, 64 times 1000 is 64000.</p>
